{"id": "216665", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=216665", "title": "Tunuy\u00e1n", "text": "Tunuy\u00e1n is a small city in the Andean foothills of western Mendoza Province. It is the heart of the Uco Valley viticultural area and wine connoisseurs come to the area to visit some of the nearly 40 local vineyards. \nUnderstand.\nThe city has a population of just under 50,000 residents (2020). \nWith average temperatures of 14 \u00b0C and elevations of 900 to 1200 meters with more than 200 days of sunshine per year, vintners find the conditions right for growing wine grapes. Grape varietals are predominately Semillon (a white grape) and Malbec (a red grape that makes Argentina's most widely exported wines). Other varietals include Bonarda and Barbera, both red grapes. Many wineries welcome visitors with vineyard tours and tastings of the local wines. Often, on-site restaurants offer dishes paired with specific wines. \nGet in.\nThe nearest airport with commercial flights is in Mendoza. \nFrom Mendoza, several bus companies operate comfortable, modern buses directly to Tunuyan. The most frequent buses are offered by Iselin or Andesmar, each with several buses per day. The 1-hour ride will cost about US$8. \nGet around.\nWineries are typically in rural areas and are unlikely to have convenient public transport. A bicycle is a good option for getting between nearby wineries, but most travelers will find it easier to rent a car. Just be careful about wine consumption and keep yourself and local residents safe."}
{"id": "216668", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=216668", "title": "\u010cesk\u00e1 Skalice", "text": "\u010cesk\u00e1 Skalice is a town in the Hradec Kr\u00e1lov\u00e9 Region of East Bohemia. It has about 5,000 inhabitants (2025). It lies on the \u00dapa River and on the shore of Rozko\u0161 Reservoir. The town is known for the Ratibo\u0159ice Castle and Grandmother's Valley, both associated with the work of one of the most important Czech women writers, Bo\u017eena N\u011bmcov\u00e1.\nGet in.\n\u010cesk\u00e1 Skalice is located about 8 kilometres (5 mi) west of N\u00e1chod and 24 km (15 mi) northeast of Hradec Kr\u00e1lov\u00e9.\nThe I/33 road from Hradec Kr\u00e1lov\u00e9 to N\u00e1chod (part of the European route E67) passes next to the town.\n\u010cesk\u00e1 Skalice is located on the railway lines\u2013Prague\u2013Trutnov and Pardubice\u2013Svoboda nad \u00dapou.\nDo.\nA path called \u201cBathildina stezka\u201d (Bathilda's Path) runs into the valley from the ch\u00e2teau park. On the way to the mill, you will pass along the high brick wall of the former manorial garden called \u201cKv\u011btnice\u201d (Flower Garden) of 1801."}
{"id": "216673", "revid": "1423298", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=216673", "title": "Dv\u016fr Kr\u00e1lov\u00e9 nad Labem", "text": "Dv\u016fr Kr\u00e1lov\u00e9 nad Labem is a town in the Hradec Kr\u00e1lov\u00e9 Region of East Bohemia. It has about 15,000 inhabitants (2025). It lies in the Elbe river valley. Dv\u016fr Kr\u00e1lov\u00e9 nad Labem is known for the Safari Park Dv\u016fr Kr\u00e1lov\u00e9, one of the largest zoos in the country. The historic town centre is well preserved and is protected as an urban monument zone.\nGet in.\nDv\u016fr Kr\u00e1lov\u00e9 nad Labem is located about 16 kilometres (10 mi) southwest of Trutnov and 24 km (15 mi) north of Hradec Kr\u00e1lov\u00e9. There is no direct train connection. From Prague, you can transfer in Hradec Kr\u00e1lov\u00e9; from Brno, the transfer point is in Pardubice (ride time is about 3 hr in both cases).\nSee.\nThe historic core is formed by T. G. Masaryka Square. Its main landmark is the Renaissance Old Town Hall. It was built in 1833, after the original building from 1572 burned down in 1790. It has arcades and decorative fa\u00e7ade. Other sights of the square include Art Nouveau savings bank from 1909\u20131910, Baroque marian column from 1754, and a fountain from 1857.\nIn the town part of \u017dire\u010d there is an old residence of the Jesuits."}
